  "limitations": [
    "DIRECTORY-LISTING METADATA EXPOSURE (non-semantic). During initial orientation the checker ran a directory listing that included producer/ and producer-support/. Only filenames, byte sizes and modification timestamps were returned; no file content from either directory was opened. Two producer-support filenames contain topical words. No producer disposition, boundary, reasoning, exception list or distribution was exposed. Disclosed rather than suppressed.",
    "PROSE STAGE-ID ABBREVIATION. In 51 rows the narrative evidence text refers to a stage by an abbreviated prefix (for example 'stage_1' where the declared id is 'stage_1_infusion_reaction'). A mechanical cross-check confirmed every such abbreviation resolves to exactly one declared stage of that row's own parent, with zero ambiguous or cross-parent cases, and every proposedBoundary value is an exact declared stage id. This is prose imprecision only; no disposition is affected.",
    "ONE DISCLOSED AMENDMENT. repair-012 was rewritten before the complete freeze to correct a checker transcription error in a single confidence field that contradicted the checker's own recorded reasoning. The superseded hash is retained in the packet freeze chain and in 'amendments'. No disposition, boundary, evidence text or identity field changed.",
    "BASELINE-HEAVY DISTRIBUTION IS A CONTENT PROPERTY, NOT A DEFAULT. 423 of 451 rows resolved to BASELINE. The recurring structural reason, documented per row, is that in this corpus the part itself (stem, options, matrix rows, cloze sentences, highlight segments) routinely restates the stage data it refers to, frequently carrying its own baseline comparator, while the stage exhibits frequently narrate the nurse performing the keyed action or state the keyed answer verbatim in both languages. Under R4's earliest-answerability rule a stage that supplies nothing the answer needs is not a legitimate boundary. No positional, title, timestamp, sibling-anchor or first/final-stage rule was used.",
    "ITEM-LEVEL DISCLOSURES OBSERVED BUT NOT ACTED ON. Several parents disclose their own answer on the baseline surface through the case title (for example titles naming 'Acute hemolytic transfusion reaction', 'AMI with Cardiogenic Shock', 'Refeeding syndrome', 'preeclampsia with severe features'). R4 counts the title as baseline-visible, so these were treated as pre-existing item-design features and recorded in the affected rows' evidence rather than repaired; R4 forbids content change.",
    "THREE NON-HIGH ROWS. Three rows carry MEDIUM confidence with the counter-argument stated in the row evidence. Under R4 section E.1 a non-HIGH result cannot pass the acceptance gate regardless of agreement, so these are expected to become final exceptions.",
    "ONE EXPLICIT EXCEPTION. Row 25b7ff4311e66f43 is an unresolvable-ambiguity exception, not an unfinished row; the reason is recorded in exceptionReason.",
    "SCOPE OF THIS FREEZE. Completeness here means all 451 frozen rows were independently reviewed and frozen. It does not assert agreement with the producer, does not assert that any row is patchable, and does not constitute acceptance."
  ],
